  "Zero-cost arm is a diagnostic rung (the arm the family sign was read at), not a tradeable configuration.",
  "The null runs on THIS panel only. It can show that the family's direction is the direction noise produces, but only a null on the family panel can price the family's own width effect (that is the next round, not a claim made here)."
 ],
 "statement": "Family reading (quoted): wider books earned [0.685, 0.73, 0.77, 1.14, 1.56]pp more per rung at rank corr 1.0 inside a 1653-name pool. On the 18-name cross: the sign does not travel -- it flips on this panel (cagr rank corr -1.0 at 0.0bp, -1.0 at 8.0bp), so the width direction is that family's naming, not a portable mechanism. Random-score control (N=160 runs): real-minus-null [11.51, 7.28, 5.92, 3.3]pp across widths (rank corr -1.0), so the width sign belongs to the score, not to noise. The quoted family direction (1.0) is the same direction the noise arm takes on this panel (1.0), so the family width sign is not yet evidence about the signal: it needs its own null."
